<title>RUSSIA: Russia Norilsk Nickel shares up 10.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia Norilsk Nickel shares up 10.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Russian metal group Norilsk Nickel had risen 10.8 percent to $14.85 at 0952 GMT on the Russian Trading System on Wednesday from $13.40 at the previous close.</p>
<p>Auction bidding for a 38 percent controlling stake managed by UNEXIM Bank began on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Pref shares had risen to $10.63 from $9.75.</p>
<p>Both were among the top 10 most-traded shares. Just under $3 million of ordinary shares and over $500,000 prefs had turned over after almost three hours of trade.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
